{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "budget-two-steps-reranker", "category": "budget_pressure_partial", "question": "Describe the reranker briefly?", "max_steps": 2, "top_k": 1, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/retrieval.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["reranking-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 1, "expects_repeated_evidence": false, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "The uncovered-terms follow-up spends the second step and retrieves nothing, exhausting a two-step budget while one passage is grounded."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "budget-one-step-reranking", "category": "budget_pressure_partial", "question": "Explain reranking.", "max_steps": 1, "top_k": 1, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/retrieval.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["reranking-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 1, "expects_repeated_evidence": false, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "One step, score 2, budget spent: a partial report with one citation."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "budget-one-step-refusal-passage", "category": "budget_pressure_partial", "question": "What is a refusal?", "max_steps": 1, "top_k": 1, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/answers.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["refusal-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 1, "expects_repeated_evidence": false, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "One step, score 2, budget spent."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "budget-one-step-marker", "category": "budget_pressure_partial", "question": "Define a marker precisely?", "max_steps": 1, "top_k": 1, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/answers.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["citations-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 1, "expects_repeated_evidence": false, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "One step retrieves the citations passage; score 2 with no budget left."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "budget-two-steps-fusion", "category": "budget_pressure_partial", "question": "Explain fusion once?", "max_steps": 2, "top_k": 1, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/retrieval.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["hybrid-retrieval-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 1, "expects_repeated_evidence": false, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "Step one grounds the hybrid passage, step two spends the budget on the uncovered-terms follow-up and finds nothing."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "budget-two-steps-refusal-rule", "category": "budget_pressure_partial", "question": "Restate the refusal rule?", "max_steps": 2, "top_k": 1, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/answers.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["refusal-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 1, "expects_repeated_evidence": false, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "Same shape at a two-step budget with the refusal passage as the grounded evidence."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "budget-one-step-wide-top-k", "category": "budget_pressure_partial", "question": "Describe the shortlist now?", "max_steps": 1, "top_k": 5, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/retrieval.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["reranking-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 1, "expects_repeated_evidence": false, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "A wide top_k does not rescue a one-step budget when only one passage overlaps: the cap is an upper bound on what a step may return, not a floor."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "duplicate-evidence-chunking-twice", "category": "duplicate_evidence", "question": "Explain chunking thoroughly and explain chunking in the Patagonia quarterly ledger", "max_steps": 3, "top_k": 5, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/ingest.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["chunking-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 2, "expects_repeated_evidence": true, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "Both planned sub-questions retrieve the same chunking passage. The state keeps it once, so two steps of evidence produce exactly one citation — the case that would catch thin evidence being counted as corroborated."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "duplicate-evidence-shortlist-twice", "category": "duplicate_evidence", "question": "Describe the shortlist and describe the shortlist for a violin bow sold at auction", "max_steps": 3, "top_k": 1, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/retrieval.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["reranking-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 2, "expects_repeated_evidence": true, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "Both fragments share the single corpus term 'shortlist', so both steps return the reranking passage and the state stores it once."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "duplicate-evidence-refusal-twice", "category": "duplicate_evidence", "question": "What does refusal mean in Ushuaia and what does refusal mean at a violin auction?", "max_steps": 3, "top_k": 1, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/answers.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["refusal-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 2, "expects_repeated_evidence": true, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "'refusal' is the only corpus term in either fragment, so both steps return the same passage."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "duplicate-evidence-heading-twice", "category": "duplicate_evidence", "question": "Explain the heading of a marathon result then explain the heading of a violin auction", "max_steps": 3, "top_k": 1, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/ingest.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["chunking-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 2, "expects_repeated_evidence": true, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "A 'then'-joined pair whose only corpus term is 'heading'; both steps return the chunking passage."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "duplicate-evidence-fusion-twice", "category": "duplicate_evidence", "question": "Which ranking does fusion combine and which ranking does fusion combine for a violin auction?", "max_steps": 3, "top_k": 5, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/retrieval.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["hybrid-retrieval-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 2, "expects_repeated_evidence": true, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "'fusion' is the only corpus term; a wide top_k changes nothing because only one passage overlaps at all."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "duplicate-evidence-marker-twice", "category": "duplicate_evidence", "question": "How is a marker used in a brisket cookbook and how is a marker used at a violin auction?", "max_steps": 3, "top_k": 1, "expected_terminal_status": "budget_exhausted", "expected_stop_reason": "budget_spent", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/answers.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["citations-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 2, "expects_repeated_evidence": true, "normalization_group": null, "rationale": "'marker' is the only corpus term in either fragment; both steps return the citations passage."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "normalization-fusion-plain", "category": "text_normalization", "question": "Which two rankings does fusion combine?", "max_steps": 4, "top_k": 5, "expected_terminal_status": "done", "expected_stop_reason": "evidence_sufficient", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/retrieval.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["hybrid-retrieval-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 1, "expects_repeated_evidence": false, "normalization_group": "fusion-case", "rationale": "Baseline surface form. The tokeniser lowercases before splitting on non-alphanumeric characters, so its uppercase twin must produce the same terms and therefore the same run."}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "id": "normalization-fusion-uppercase", "category": "text_normalization", "question": "WHICH TWO RANKINGS DOES FUSION COMBINE?", "max_steps": 4, "top_k": 5, "expected_terminal_status": "done", "expected_stop_reason": "evidence_sufficient", "expected_min_citations": 1, "expected_max_citations": 1, "expected_source_paths": ["docs/retrieval.md"], "expected_chunk_ids": ["hybrid-retrieval-1"], "expected_min_plan_size": 1, "expects_repeated_evidence": false, "normalization_group": "fusion-case", "rationale": "Uppercase twin of the plain form; case is folded before scoring, so any divergence is a tokeniser regression."}
